{**
 * c-notice - one sentence the page has to say to whoever is reading it: that
 * something was saved, or that something was refused.
 *
 * The variant names what kind of news it is rather than what colour it should
 * be, so a theme decides how loud either one looks. A refusal is announced to a
 * screen reader as soon as it appears, because somebody who cannot see the page
 * change would otherwise be left with a form that simply did nothing.
 *
 * A dismissible notice carries c-close, and pressing it hides the notice
 * (assets/notice.ts). The live region is then the sentence alone rather than
 * the whole notice, because a region holding the button would announce
 * "Saved. Dismiss" every time it appeared. A notice that is not dismissible is
 * drawn exactly as it always was.
 *
 * A notice with a title says what happened over the sentence that says what to
 * do about it - a page that was not published, and why. The title and the
 * sentence are one live region, announced together, because a title read out
 * on its own says that something happened and not what. The title is not a
 * heading: the notice cannot know where in the outline of the page it is drawn,
 * and a heading at the wrong level is worse than none. A dismissible notice
 * with a title is refused until a page needs one: its live region is the
 * sentence alone, and the title would have to join it.
 *}

{import 'close.latte'}

{define notice, string $message, string $variant = 'info', ?string $testId = null, bool $dismissible = false, ?string $title = null}
    {do Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Component\Argument::holds(
        !$dismissible || $title === null,
        sprintf("c-notice '%s' is dismissible and has a title; it can be one or the other.", $message),
    )}

    <div
        n:if="$dismissible"
        n:class="'c-notice', 'c-notice--dismissible', $variant === 'danger' ? 'c-notice--danger'"
        data-testid="{$testId}"
    >
        <p class="c-notice__message" role="{$variant === 'danger' ? 'alert' : 'status'}">{$message}</p>
        {include close, label: 'Dismiss'}
    </div>
    <div
        n:elseif="$title !== null"
        n:class="'c-notice', 'c-notice--titled', $variant === 'danger' ? 'c-notice--danger'"
        role="{$variant === 'danger' ? 'alert' : 'status'}"
        data-testid="{$testId}"
    >
        <p class="c-notice__title">{$title}</p>
        <p class="c-notice__message">{$message}</p>
    </div>
    <p
        n:else
        n:class="'c-notice', $variant === 'danger' ? 'c-notice--danger'"
        role="{$variant === 'danger' ? 'alert' : 'status'}"
        data-testid="{$testId}"
    >{$message}</p>
{/define}
